1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,510
Welcome to the updated Orders Shop, the web
front end for the Orders API.

2
00:00:05,510 --> 00:00:10,130
It now has a fresh look, built with
Bootstrap and the Lumen theme,

3
00:00:10,130 --> 00:00:13,770
and it asks you to confirm before
it saves anything.

4
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:17,970
This tour uses the real app, running
locally with demo data.

5
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:22,240
We start as a customer, and then
switch to the administrator.

6
00:00:24,006 --> 00:00:25,806
This is the sign-in page.

7
00:00:25,806 --> 00:00:28,830
A new customer starts with Create account.

8
00:00:29,542 --> 00:00:35,249
Registration asks for a name, an email, and
a password, in floating labels.

9
00:00:35,249 --> 00:00:41,564
The form checks as you type, so a password that
is too short is flagged right away,

10
00:00:41,564 --> 00:00:43,390
before anything is sent.

11
00:00:44,097 --> 00:00:49,308
The password needs at least fifteen
characters, with no composition rules,

12
00:00:49,308 --> 00:00:50,927
and spaces are allowed.

13
00:00:50,927 --> 00:00:53,110
So a short sentence works well.

14
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:57,476
Then a confirmation dialog asks
whether to create the account,

15
00:00:57,476 --> 00:01:00,081
and nothing is sent until we say yes.

16
00:01:00,782 --> 00:01:04,469
The result is always the same
check your email message,

17
00:01:04,469 --> 00:01:07,820
whether or not the address was
already registered.

18
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:10,166
That keeps account lookups private.

19
00:01:10,877 --> 00:01:15,229
If you try to sign in before
confirming, the app explains why,

20
00:01:15,229 --> 00:01:18,317
and offers to resend the
confirmation email.

21
00:01:19,019 --> 00:01:21,853
In this local setup, email is simulated,

22
00:01:21,853 --> 00:01:25,750
and the confirmation link is
written to the server log.

23
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:28,018
Opening it confirms the address,

24
00:01:28,018 --> 00:01:32,411
and the app removes the token from the
address bar right away.

25
00:01:33,118 --> 00:01:35,230
Now the customer can sign in.

26
00:01:38,633 --> 00:01:43,297
Signed-in customers land on the
catalog: eight demo products,

27
00:01:43,297 --> 00:01:46,049
each with a price and a stock state.

28
00:01:46,753 --> 00:01:51,243
Search matches name or SKU, and
starts after two characters.

29
00:01:51,243 --> 00:01:53,414
One letter only shows a hint.

30
00:01:53,414 --> 00:01:58,428
Typing key narrows the list, and the
search is kept in the address,

31
00:01:58,428 --> 00:02:00,673
so the page can be bookmarked.

32
00:02:01,372 --> 00:02:03,445
Sorting and filters work too.

33
00:02:03,445 --> 00:02:06,877
Here the list runs from most to
least expensive,

34
00:02:06,877 --> 00:02:11,524
limited to products under one hundred
dollars, and in stock only.

35
00:02:12,239 --> 00:02:15,446
Opening a product shows its
details and stock,

36
00:02:15,446 --> 00:02:18,863
with a quantity picker and an
add to cart button.

37
00:02:19,569 --> 00:02:23,322
Let's add the keyboard with the
green Add to cart button,

38
00:02:23,322 --> 00:02:25,955
and then a wireless mouse from the list.

39
00:02:25,955 --> 00:02:29,049
The cart count in the header
updates each time.

40
00:02:29,755 --> 00:02:34,020
In the cart, quantities can be
changed and products removed,

41
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:36,295
and the estimated total follows.

42
00:02:36,295 --> 00:02:40,915
The cart lives in this browser, and is
cleared when you sign out.

43
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:47,826
Placing the order asks for confirmation first,
then checks current prices and stock,

44
00:02:47,826 --> 00:02:49,526
and sends it just once.

45
00:02:49,526 --> 00:02:54,328
The new order opens right away as
pending, with its items, total,

46
00:02:54,328 --> 00:02:55,732
and status history.

47
00:02:56,439 --> 00:03:02,131
My orders lists every order, with filters for
status and dates, and sorting.

48
00:03:02,131 --> 00:03:05,127
The filters stay in the address as well.

49
00:03:05,838 --> 00:03:09,825
A pending order can be cancelled,
with an optional reason.

50
00:03:09,825 --> 00:03:13,950
The status changes to cancelled, and
the history records it.

51
00:03:14,659 --> 00:03:16,841
My account shows the profile.

52
00:03:16,841 --> 00:03:18,571
The email is read only.

53
00:03:18,571 --> 00:03:22,408
Edit profile changes the name
and the phone number.

54
00:03:22,408 --> 00:03:26,696
Save changes stays disabled until
something is different,

55
00:03:26,696 --> 00:03:29,179
and saving asks for confirmation.

56
00:03:29,888 --> 00:03:33,206
Changing the password asks for
confirmation too.

57
00:03:33,206 --> 00:03:38,528
It then signs you out on every device, so you
sign in again with the new one.

58
00:03:43,534 --> 00:03:48,094
Sign out everywhere ends the sessions
on all devices at once.

59
00:03:48,796 --> 00:03:52,762
If you forget the password, enter
the email, confirm,

60
00:03:52,762 --> 00:03:55,455
and you always see the same message.

61
00:03:55,455 --> 00:04:01,516
The reset link, again from the server log,
opens a page to choose a new password.

62
00:04:01,516 --> 00:04:05,332
After one more confirmation, you
return to sign-in.

63
00:04:06,231 --> 00:04:08,947
Customers cannot open the back office.

64
00:04:08,947 --> 00:04:12,591
The admin address shows a
not-allowed page instead.

65
00:04:13,297 --> 00:04:15,888
Delete account explains what happens.

66
00:04:15,888 --> 00:04:20,440
Personal details are erased, order
records are kept without them,

67
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:22,471
and you cannot sign in again.

68
00:04:22,471 --> 00:04:26,113
It asks for the current password
and a confirmation.

69
00:04:26,814 --> 00:04:30,558
Afterwards, the same
credentials no longer work.

70
00:04:33,935 --> 00:04:38,926
Administrators sign in on the same page,
and land in the back office.

71
00:04:38,926 --> 00:04:44,351
The dashboard shows the low-stock count, and
the last thirty days of sales.

72
00:04:45,063 --> 00:04:50,844
The Products section lists every product,
with search, sorting, and paging.

73
00:04:50,844 --> 00:04:56,703
The Edit button is yellow and Delete is red,
so the risky action stands out.

74
00:04:57,407 --> 00:05:01,044
Creating a product validates
the form first.

75
00:05:01,044 --> 00:05:07,823
Then the name, SKU, description, price, and
stock are saved, after a confirmation.

76
00:05:09,352 --> 00:05:14,179
Editing loads the latest version and
saves with a concurrency check,

77
00:05:14,179 --> 00:05:17,799
so two admins cannot silently
overwrite each other.

78
00:05:17,799 --> 00:05:19,432
Here I raise the stock.

79
00:05:20,134 --> 00:05:22,390
Deleting asks for confirmation.

80
00:05:22,390 --> 00:05:26,393
It is a soft delete: customers
stop seeing the product,

81
00:05:26,393 --> 00:05:29,086
and existing orders keep their lines.

82
00:05:29,796 --> 00:05:33,972
With Include deleted ticked, the
product shows as deleted,

83
00:05:33,972 --> 00:05:35,844
and one click restores it.

84
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:42,619
That is the customer portal, and the
first part of the back office.

85
00:05:42,619 --> 00:05:45,927
Screens for customers, orders,
reports, users,

86
00:05:45,927 --> 00:05:49,092
and audit logs are not in the
interface yet.

87
00:05:49,092 --> 00:05:52,256
For now those are available
through the API.

88
00:05:52,256 --> 00:05:57,938
To try it yourself, start the stack with
docker compose up, and open localhost,

89
00:05:57,938 --> 00:05:59,808
port eight zero eight one.
